    "details": "<p><strong>Fight. Adapt. Win.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Battlecode</strong> is a competitive programming challenge by the IEEE CS Chapter that combines algorithmic problem-solving with strategic gameplay.</li>\n<li>Designed for students who enjoy coding under pressure, the event tests your DSA, logical reasoning, debugging, problem-solving, strategy and time-management skills through multiple rounds of increasing difficulty.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Event Structure:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Round 0 &mdash; The Warm-Up:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Get familiar with the competition format and put your problem-solving skills to the test with an introductory coding challenge.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Round 1 &mdash; The Challenge:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Go head-to-head in 1v1 coding battles.</li>\n<li>Face another participant, solve algorithmic problems under strict time constraints and race to outscore your opponent.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Round 2 &mdash; The Battle:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Push your coding and strategic thinking further as the competition intensifies.</li>\n<li>Adapt to your opponents, make smart decisions and fight your way up the leaderboard.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Round 3 &mdash; The Final Showdown:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Face the toughest challenges of the competition, followed by a hacking phase where you can test and break other participants' solutions using carefully designed test cases.</li>\n<li>Outsmart your opponents and fight for the top spot.</li>\n<li>Whether you are a seasoned competitive programmer or someone looking to challenge your coding abilities, Battlecode is an opportunity to compete, think strategically and solve problems under pressure.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Event Details:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Date: 18 September 2026</li>\n<li>Time: 10:00 AM &ndash; 6:00 PM</li>\n<li>Eligibility: Open to all college students</li>\n<li>Participants must solve all challenges independently.</li>\n<li>The use of AI tools, internet resources, documentation, external references, additional devices or assistance from other participants is strictly prohibited during the competition.</li>\n<li>You can complete the payment here after registering on Unstop: <a href=\"http://gravitas.vit.ac.in/events/4160a46a-3701-4622-8e7c-66909769704b\">gravitas.vit.ac.in/events/4160a46a-3701-4622-8e7c-66909769704b</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Are you ready to enter the battle and prove your coding skills?</strong></p>",
